{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/846617-earthbound-and-corpses","id":846617,"title":"Earthbound and corpses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-13T09:58:25-07:00","id":846617,"title":"Earthbound and corpses","content":"Now, I am going to be doing it anyway, because I am a storyteller and I get to make shit up if I need to, but in the books, could an Earthbound possess a corpse as it's reliquary? Are there powers that could make it move and talk as though it were the actual person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T10:16:59-07:00","id":846623,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but I would rule it that it can't preserve the corpse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T10:26:07-07:00","id":846625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/846617-earthbound-and-corpses?p=846623#post846623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but I would rule it that it can't preserve the corpse</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was thinking he could use an illusion to mask the rotting appearance and a lot of cologne for the smell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T14:37:56-07:00","id":846724,"title":"","content":"It would easier a statue with movable parts/pieces, like a iron skeleton for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T20:13:37-07:00","id":846891,"title":"","content":"Maybe, but it is specifically desecrating the corpse of a PC's family member.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T22:58:37-07:00","id":846952,"title":"","content":"Hi, keywords: intention and meaning<br /> human bodies are frail and suffer multiple weaknesses. The best example that can convey the idea of &quot;Earthbound posessing a Human Carcass&quot; is the movie &quot;End of Days&quot; AkA Arnold Vs The Devil.<br /> Rules to use this.<br /> One: The main rule coming with Earthbounds is Meaning. They Can Not possess something with out meaning, Example, Vei'ltharxhzorn Angel of Ashes CANT use Carl's (his loyal follower) Preparation H as a vessel. It must have a poetical ritualistic sense, no matter how twisted it is, same happends to human vessels.<br /> <br /> lets say that Erm'ger'xerz -Angel of The Outer Void- wants to take over a human body, Its decide to take over Hobo Steve. What would happend?, hobo's steve body would explode right away. Gib Everywhere, nothing happend...Why? because Hobo Steve isnt special. Not in the &quot;Mommy and Daddy think youre special:&quot; way, but in the &quot;What limp bizkit did to music on the 2000s&quot; kind of special (fuck'ed things up). The vessel must be something with a bigger significance, a being born on a special date under certain conditions, a ritualistic birth at the 6/6/6 while the equinox or something similar.<br /> <br /> Second: How to &quot;Defeat&quot; the human vessel? three ways.<br /> Dakka, Fire , decayment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:45:34-07:00","id":847143,"title":"","content":"It's effectively a question of whether the body is just another kind of object or it still has vestiges of personhood.<br /> <br /> That would be a tough question if the &quot;universe&quot; were more relative in Demon, but, it's Demon, so it's not. The general rules from the various source materials from which Demon derives would provide the guidelines. In which case, a body isn't a part of the dead person (not like with the Egyptians, etc.), it's a special type of object about which there are A LOT of taboos. That probably means it would be like trying possess an object with specific attributions (a lot of which have to do with &quot;pollution&quot;) attached, but not necessarily ones inimical to profane beings like Earthbound. But it might not be possible to possess SOME bodies. Like, say, there is a specific period of time in which the ghost is supposed to be present and your interpretation is that the dead soul still has some claim on the form, that may be enough like a living person that an Earthbound can't do it for all the reasons that Earthbound can't manage decent possession and integration with humans.<br /> <br /> However, I would probably make a body somewhere between say, a rock or a book or trying to possess a person. In general, the better prepared the body the longer it lasts. Having an Earthbound inside would probably corrupt a body pretty fast in any case. So, a REALLY fresh just dead corpse maybe just hours, even. Wait until starts to rot and you get days. Get it embalmed or otherwise specially preserved and probably weeks (particularly with the foulness that is modern embalming... essentially bodies are toxic waste afterwards). If the body was specially prepared, to be the host of the Earthbound it might last as long as any other Reliquary.<br /> <br /> One particularly icky thought is having the Earthbound try to &quot;upgrade&quot; it's home. E.g. It inhabits a fresh corpse, but runs off and to the mortician and gets itself embalmed. Ya know, on the table with the all the surgical type bits going on while the blood is being exchanged for preservative. The whole time it is participating in a ceremony with its cultists or just instructing various minions on their tasks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:37:56-07:00","id":847184,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not, but it should come with its own set of advantages and disadvantages. Like say have a reliquary corpse have and advantage of being mobile, allow the earthbound to access their urges freely, and able to heal by spending 1 faith per health level, but lack the resilience of a normal reliquary(mortal bodies are fragile), and require constant care to keep it from rotting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T03:58:46-07:00","id":847606,"title":"","content":"The story is that the Vampire lost his twin brother (who was his ghoul), got the body preserved by the Giovanni and then performed a ritual to summon a demon to bargain to restore life to his brother. The demon twisted it by taking possession of the corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T17:24:55-07:00","id":847936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/846617-earthbound-and-corpses?p=847606#post847606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The story is that the Vampire lost his twin brother (who was his ghoul), got the body preserved by the Giovanni and then performed a ritual to summon a demon to bargain to restore life to his brother. The demon twisted it by taking possession of the corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which demon is it?<br /> <br /> The decayment process might go from a couple of days to months depending On who is it.<br /> <br /> Is The brain intact? The demon would use The body until its not longer Useful. If The demon can work without 70% of his body, then he is still game On.<br /> <br /> Remember: think as if was a Terminator. Make sure he no longer is capable of working. So, fire ,Crushing. Electricity and bullets wont do much, same with stabbing. He might develop Rituals to keep himself &quot;Fresh&quot; but... Think Frank of Hellraiser","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:35:53-07:00","id":848225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/846617-earthbound-and-corpses?p=847606#post847606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The story is that the Vampire lost his twin brother (who was his ghoul), got the body preserved by the Giovanni and then performed a ritual to summon a demon to bargain to restore life to his brother. The demon twisted it by taking possession of the corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Typically this would just make the corpse &quot;alive&quot; again as the demon possesses it(as per DTF rules). I thought you meant actually going through the process of making a body into an unliving reliquary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:15:08-07:00","id":848323,"title":"","content":"For just regular possession/inhabitation, doesn't the Earthbound sourcebook already have rules for possessing human bodies? As in, they quickly get burned up (a process which would probably only be accelerated in the case of an already dead body).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:39:47-07:00","id":848561,"title":"","content":"Yeah in the books they can possess someone for about 48 hours. This is much longer term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:51:23-07:00","id":848567,"title":"","content":"If I was running this I would only have the illusions effect everyone else but the pc, who gets to deal with the horror that maybe it's all in his mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T03:13:55-07:00","id":848702,"title":"","content":"It seems like it would make most sense to simply treat the corpse as just an object- inanimate dead flesh possessed in the same vein as any material for an Improvised or Perfect (if specially ritually prepared/embalmed/embellished) Reliquary, accruing all the timeless resilience that would characterize such a vessel and with the same criteria (e.g. strong personal or cultic significance) for being a valid subject for possession. One idea that occurred me to a while back was an Earthbound being summoned into the preserved and ritually desecrated corpse of a saint as his Perfect Reliquary. The soul is already fled and you're taking the flesh as a house for your essence, rather than the being as an active and mobile vehicle for your power and will. You don't get the perks of Urges, mobility and physical action, cheap Apocalyptic Form usage, etc. but you also won't casually burn it out, either. Without a soul, the human body is just an assemblage of matter like any other object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 03-17-2016, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:18:58-07:00","id":848810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/846617-earthbound-and-corpses?p=848702#post848702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like it would make most sense to simply treat the corpse as just an object- inanimate dead flesh possessed in the same vein as any material for an Improvised or Perfect (if specially ritually prepared/embalmed/embellished) Reliquary, accruing all the timeless resilience that would characterize such a vessel and with the same criteria (e.g. strong personal or cultic significance) for being a valid subject for possession. One idea that occurred me to a while back was an Earthbound being summoned into the preserved and ritually desecrated corpse of a saint as his Perfect Reliquary. The soul is already fled and you're taking the flesh as a house for your essence, rather than the being as an active and mobile vehicle for your power and will. You don't get the perks of Urges, mobility and physical action, cheap Apocalyptic Form usage, etc. but you also won't casually burn it out, either. Without a soul, the human body is just an assemblage of matter like any other object.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This sounds like something you could base an entire campaign around, either trying to stop an earthbound from acquiring said super form or, failing that, trying to put the demi-god bastard down.No easy task considering any sufficiently strong earthbound is on par with a methuselah(or an ante if we're talking the big 5) in terms of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:54:16-07:00","id":849001,"title":"","content":"in devil due this is actually possible(with the appropriate arcana) however i do recall that it had some sort of disadvantage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T12:09:53-07:00","id":849381,"title":"","content":"Chapter 3 in Devil's Due , specifically the Torment and Taint system would be a good way to handle it if you want to detailed. For my part, if its an NPC I'd simply roll 1 die every scene the npc at a difficulty of 9 that drops by 1 if sometime in the scene the Earthbound uses a Lore, engages in conflict with the pc's, or fails to upkeep its corpse-body. On a success remove a Health Level and describe how the body is slightly more rotten, leaking auras of damnation, faintly glowing of infernal power etc.<br /> <br /> Your pcs will pick up on the rot, instability, etc. And it will pace it out based on the story instead of some arbitrary time frame.<br /> <br /> I did something like this in a Mage the Ascension game, the demon was bound to a corpse by way of a nail driven through the forehead of the ritually prepared body. The nail itself was a reliquary that bound the soul to the body. One PCs backstory was they dabbled in infernalism and beat a demon at its own game, when the demon walked into a cafe they frequented, it was pretty great.<br /> <br /> Eventually the dabbler went to hell to take the demon with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}